---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { tools, verticals, rankToolsForVertical, verticalFitScore, wrenchStackScore } from '../lib/data';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
  { name: 'Disclosure', url: '/disclosure/' },
];

// Computed (2026-10-01). The page claimed "tools we earn $10,000 per signup on"
// (no program on the ledger pays that) and that unaffiliated tools "regularly" outrank
// them; both are replaced by counts from the data. "Active" uses the same test as the
// methodology ledger: a tracked http affiliate_url.
const isActive = (t: (typeof tools)[number]) => t.affiliate_url.startsWith('http');
const activeCount = tools.filter(isActive).length;
// A trade counts when none of the tools tied for first place on its trade page
// (same trade fit and same Fit Score as the first-ranked tool) has a tracked link.
const tradesTopUnaffiliated = verticals.filter((v) => {
  const ranked = rankToolsForVertical(v.slug);
  if (!ranked.length) return false;
  const top = ranked[0];
  const topGroup = ranked.filter(
    (t) =>
      verticalFitScore(t, v.slug) === verticalFitScore(top, v.slug) &&
      wrenchStackScore(t, v.slug) === wrenchStackScore(top, v.slug)
  );
  return !topGroup.some(isActive);
}).length;
---

<Layout
  title="Disclosure: how we make money | WrenchStack"
  description="How WrenchStack makes money (commissions and referral rewards from vendor programs, and pricing benchmark reports) and how rankings are kept separate from both."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12 prose prose-slate">
    <h1>Disclosure: how we make money</h1>

    <p>WrenchStack makes money in two ways: commissions and referral rewards from vendor programs, and pricing benchmark reports sold to software vendors. Both are described on this page.</p>

    <p>
      WrenchStack may earn a commission or a referral reward when readers sign up with a vendor through a
      tracked link on our pages. Of the {tools.length} software tools in the directory, {activeCount} have a tracked affiliate
      or referral link; the <a href="/methodology/#affiliate-ledger">per-vendor ledger</a> lists the status of every one.
      Reviews in the other categories state their affiliate status on the page. The vendor pays the
      commission or reward; we add no charge of our own.
    </p>

    <h2>How affiliate relationships affect rankings</h2>

    <p>
      On each trade page, field-service software is ordered by fit for that trade, then by the
      <a href="/methodology/">WrenchStack Fit Score</a> (vertical fit 60%, pricing transparency 20%,
      integration coverage 20%), then by name. Neither the ordering nor the score has an input for
      affiliate status or commission rate. On {tradesTopUnaffiliated} of the {verticals.length} trade
      pages, none of the tools ranked first has a tracked affiliate or referral link. Lead generation, insurance,
      payroll and marketing agencies are grouped by published tier rules that use verified facts only.
    </p>

    <h2>Pricing benchmark reports</h2>

    <p>
      We also sell pricing benchmark reports to software vendors, including vendors listed on this site.
      Whether a vendor bought a report is not an input to any listing, Fit Score, ranking, award or
      reputation flag, or to whether a product is listed. Each sale is listed in the
      <a href="/methodology/#report-ledger">report ledger</a> with the buyer's Fit Score, rank, award and
      reputation flag when it ordered and today, and is noted on the buyer's tool page and on the trade pages
      that list it. The price, the rules and the <a href="/report-terms/">report terms</a> are linked from the
      <a href="/for-vendors/#reports">vendor page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>FTC disclosure</h2>

    <p>
      The FTC's
      <a href="https://www.ftc.gov/business-guidance/resources/disclosures-101-social-media-influencers">Endorsement Guides</a>
      call for clear disclosure of material connections such as affiliate commissions. This page, the
      per-vendor ledger, the report ledger and the disclosures on each review and trade page are how we disclose ours.
      Affiliate links use <code>rel="sponsored"</code> in the page source. Outbound CTAs use
      <code>nofollow noopener</code> for security and search engine signaling.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>

    <p>
      Email <a href="mailto:hello@wrenchstack.com">hello@wrenchstack.com</a> for corrections or
      clarifications. For vendor listings and affiliate questions, use <a href="mailto:partners@wrenchstack.com">partners@wrenchstack.com</a>; for pricing benchmark report orders, <a href="mailto:bilal@wrenchstack.com?subject=Report%20order">bilal@wrenchstack.com</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
